1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,040
The sixth habit that's been really powerful in my own self improvement journey has been this concept of constant education.
第六个对我自我提升之旅很有力量的习惯，是持续学习这个概念。

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:18,240
So it's constantly learning and I feel like once you start this journey you realize you know it's that famous saying uh the more you know the more you realize you don't know.
也就是不断学习。我感觉，一旦开始这段旅程，你会意识到那句名言：知道得越多，越发现自己不知道的也越多。

3
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:25,240
And it's so true I think learning about ourselves and becoming better as a person is a lifelong pursuit.
这真是这样。我认为，认识自己、成为更好的人，是一生的追求。

4
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:33,480
I I don't think we'll ever get to a stage where we're just done you know like we feel like we've accomplished or learned everything there is to learn about ourselves.
我不认为我们会到达一个“已经完成”的阶段，觉得自己已经实现或学完了关于自己的一切。

5
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:37,281
I really do think we could do that until our very last day.
我确实觉得，我们可以一直做这件事，直到生命的最后一天。

6
00:00:37,281 --> 00:00:43,441
And so being engaged in constant education which you're probably already doing if you're listening to this podcast.
所以，投入持续学习——如果你在听这个播客，你可能已经在做了——

7
00:00:43,441 --> 00:00:54,401
But through podcasts through books through interesting articles through reading papers whatever you find inspiring whatever gets you thinking actually having that as a habit.
通过播客、书籍、有趣的文章、论文，任何让你受到启发、促使你思考的东西，真正把它变成习惯。

8
00:00:54,401 --> 00:00:57,401
So not just ad hockly when you feel like it having as a habit.
而不是只在想起来时“ad hockly”地做；要把它当作习惯（字幕表达待核）。

9
00:00:57,401 --> 00:01:02,271
For example uh monday mornings when you're walking on the treadmill that's your time to learn something new.
比如，周一早晨在跑步机上走路时，就是你学习新东西的时间。

10
00:01:02,281 --> 00:01:06,560
I do do that actually on a thursday it's my 60 minute walk day.
我自己确实这么做，不过是在周四；那天是我走路六十分钟的日子。

11
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:12,601
And I always listen to a podcast on something I am interested to learn about at that period in time.
我总会听一个播客，内容是我在那段时间有兴趣了解的事。

12
00:01:12,601 --> 00:01:18,360
And and that topic area or the theme of that changes depending on what stage I'm at in life.
而那个话题领域或主题，会随着我处在人生的哪个阶段而变化。

13
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:26,240
For example now it's a lot around pregnancy having babies it's it's really just firming out my understanding in that area.
比如现在，很多内容与怀孕和生孩子有关，其实是在巩固我对那个领域的理解（原字幕用 firming out）。

14
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:31,961
Because it's something I'm interested in and something I hope you know to engage in in the next couple years of my life.
因为这是我感兴趣的事情，也希望在未来几年参与、经历这些。

15
00:01:31,961 --> 00:01:38,520
But that topic or what I choose to learn about for my own growth changes depending on where I'm at in life.
但这个话题，或者我为了成长而选择学习的内容，会随着我的人生阶段改变。

16
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:42,961
But I have that core habit of constant education.
不过，我始终保有持续学习这个核心习惯。

17
00:01:42,961 --> 00:01:51,721
So anchoring that into your week and actually having it as a regular habit is a sure way to guarantee that you're constantly evolving and growing.
所以，把它固定在一周里，真正当成固定习惯，她认为就能确保自己不断发展和成长，

18
00:01:51,721 --> 00:01:59,160
In whatever area you want to focus on confidence public speaking uh youtube whatever it is.
无论你想专注哪个领域：自信、公开演讲，还是 YouTube 等等。

19
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:07,721
The seventh type of habit that I found has been incredible for my self improvement journey is having a mindful habit.
第七种对我的自我提升很有帮助的习惯，是有一个用心觉察的习惯。

20
00:02:07,721 --> 00:02:09,881
Now I want to keep this one quite broad.
我想把这个概念保持得宽泛一些。

21
00:02:09,881 --> 00:02:15,681
And I never want to be the person to tell you that this is the habit that you need to adopt and this is how you need to do it.
我不想告诉你“这就是你必须采取的习惯，而且必须这么做”。

22
00:02:15,681 --> 00:02:20,001
Because we're all very different in terms of how we like to learn how we like to process.
因为在喜欢怎样学习、怎样消化信息这方面，我们都很不一样。

23
00:02:20,001 --> 00:02:28,201
So when I say having a mindful habit I'm talking about distraction free time and space for yourself.
因此，我所说的觉察习惯，就是留给自己不受干扰的时间和空间。

24
00:02:28,201 --> 00:02:34,601
So one could say that the phone free time that I shared before is a mindful habit.
所以可以说，我前面分享的不使用手机的时间，就是一种觉察习惯。

25
00:02:34,601 --> 00:02:42,640
But let's go a little bit deeper you know within that time you can have no phone but if you're watching netflix or doing something else and that is kind of redundant.
但再深入一点：这段时间可以不用手机，可如果你在看 Netflix 或做别的事，这就有点多余、失去意义了。

26
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,801
So what are we choosing to do in that time.
那么，我们选择在这段时间做什么呢？

27
00:02:44,801 --> 00:02:53,711
For me a mindful habit looks like meditation maybe journaling maybe just sitting there and just being with my own thoughts right thinking about them.
对我来说，觉察习惯可以是冥想、写日记，或者只是坐着，和自己的想法待在一起，想一想。

28
00:02:53,721 --> 00:02:59,361
Whatever you choose to make this mean I mean it could even be like going on a silent walk right.
无论你怎样理解这个概念，它甚至可以是出去安静地散个步。

29
00:02:59,361 --> 00:03:02,561
Where you don't have any distraction and you're just really present in the moment.
没有任何干扰，只是真正专注于当下。

30
00:03:02,561 --> 00:03:11,791
Any form of mindful habit I think is really key to anyone on a self improvement journey because you have that time with yourself.
我认为，对踏上自我提升之路的人，任何形式的觉察习惯都很关键，因为你有了与自己相处的时间。

31
00:03:11,801 --> 00:03:18,721
And if you're trying to grow and evolve as a person but you're not connected or plugged into what's actually going on in you right now.
如果你想成长、发展，却没有连接、没有接入自己此刻内心实际发生的事情，

32
00:03:18,721 --> 00:03:25,841
What you're thinking where your heads at where your mindset is reflecting on the way you you think and feel about things.
包括你在想什么、脑中是什么状态、心态如何，以及反思你对事情的想法和感受，

33
00:03:25,841 --> 00:03:32,561
You're almost operating from a point of assumption right you're you're assuming what's going on without actually plugging in.
那你几乎就是基于假设在行动，对吧？你没有真正接入自己的状态，就在假定发生了什么。

34
00:03:32,561 --> 00:03:40,121
So having a mindful habit in your routine is really important for you to establish where things are at where you're currently at.
所以，在日常安排里有一个觉察习惯，对确认现状、确认自己现在处于什么位置很重要。

35
00:03:40,121 --> 00:03:50,760
So that any efforts you make or whatever you're doing in terms of your routine or your improvement is actually reflective or matches where you're currently at.
这样，无论你做出什么努力，在习惯或自我提升上做什么，才会反映或匹配你目前的状态。
